WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.980
- There is one guy in Russia

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:03.770
that Vladimir Putin, the president,

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:06.321
fears more than anyone else.

00:00:06.321 --> 00:00:08.430
(indistinct chatter)

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:10.130
He wears a lot of different hats.

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:12.510
He's a political
activist, he's a YouTuber,

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:13.960
he's kind of an internet troll.

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:16.230
He's a lover of quality drone footage

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:18.310
to help expose corruption,

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:19.143
which like, come on,

00:00:19.143 --> 00:00:20.076
who doesn't love a good drone shot?

00:00:20.076 --> 00:00:21.410
(upbeat music playing)

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:23.860
But his main objective is singular,

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:24.990
it's very focused,

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:27.000
it's to give the Russian people

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.630
and all of us around the world,

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:30.250
a peek behind the curtain

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:32.670
to show how Russia really works.

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:36.140
Exposing the web of
bribes, corruption, lies,

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:39.300
and powerful men who really
control modern Russia.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:41.300
This important figure who is seeking

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:43.690
to dismantle Russia's web of corruption

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:45.460
is named Alexei Navalny.

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:46.480
And just last week,

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:49.030
he was sentenced to three years in jail

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:52.040
as well as being nominated
for a Nobel Peace Prize

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:54.839
after being secretly
poisoned on an airplane.

00:00:54.839 --> 00:00:57.110
(airplane whirling)

00:00:57.110 --> 00:00:58.840
The movement that he has created

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:02.770
strikes at the heart of
Vladimir Putin's biggest fears

00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:04.260
and I wanna show you why.

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:08.096
So let me introduce you to
the man Putin fears the most.

00:01:08.096 --> 00:01:09.192
- [Reporter] Alexei.
- [Reporter] Alexei.

00:01:09.192 --> 00:01:10.025
- [Reporter] Alexei.
- [Reporter] Alexei.

00:01:10.025 --> 00:01:11.305
- Russian opposition leader.

00:01:11.305 --> 00:01:12.639
- [Reporters] Alexei Navalny.

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:15.222
(upbeat music)

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:41.520
Okay, so let's rewind
to summer of last year.

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:44.480
Alexei Navalny is in a
city in Eastern Russia,

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:45.640
he's in a hotel room,

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:47.890
about to head to the
airport to catch a flight.

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:49.080
When he arrived to the airport,

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:50.400
other passengers recognize him

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:51.840
because he's kind of a big deal in Russia

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:53.080
and they snap some photos with him.

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:54.220
Then he gets on the flight,

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:55.110
the flight takes off,

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:56.560
it's a four hour flight from this

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:59.130
city of Tomsk to Moscow where he's going.

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:00.050
Everything's going normal

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:01.600
for the first 30 minutes of this flight,

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:05.030
but then Navalny starts to feel weird.

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:06.280
A flight attendant offers him

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:08.510
a bottle of water and he refuses,

00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:12.690
but soon this feeling weird
turns into severe pain.

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:16.340
(airplane whirling)

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:17.690
He runs to the laboratory

00:02:17.690 --> 00:02:19.360
looking for some reprieve.

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:21.060
He's going in and out of consciousness,

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:22.550
he may be going into a seizure,

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:24.170
his heart is slowing down,

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:26.730
his muscles are convulsing and seizing,

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:28.210
no one has any idea what's happening.

00:02:28.210 --> 00:02:32.270
A nurse aboard steps up and
helps keep him conscious

00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:35.220
while the pilots reroute
for an emergency landing

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:37.170
at a nearby city in Russia.

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:39.120
The plane lands at the closest airport

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:41.560
where medics sprint
onto the runway to help

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:43.250
only for the medics to say,

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:46.040
and I quote, this is not a case for us,

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:47.823
he needs intensive care.

00:02:50.050 --> 00:02:52.330
Navalny is then rushed to a hospital

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:54.700
but what happens inside this hospital

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:56.291
is kind of mind blowing.

00:02:56.291 --> 00:02:57.800
(cameras flashing)

00:02:57.800 --> 00:02:58.890
When he gets to the hospital,

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:00.200
they start running tests on him

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:02.000
to see what's going on.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.140
But when the doctors come looking

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:04.800
for the results of these blood tests,

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:07.070
the lab technician hands them a blood test

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:09.550
that says that Alexei
Navalny is totally fine,

00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:11.040
nothing out of the ordinary,

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:13.420
maybe a little bit of
irritable bowel issues,

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:15.250
but that's not what the doctor has seen.

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:17.193
This man looks like he has been poisoned

00:03:17.193 --> 00:03:18.980
(airplane whirling)

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:21.280
but the lab technician
didn't hand over any results

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:23.200
that indicate that he was poisoned.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:24.360
Something is up.

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:26.780
The doctors go ahead and
go with their instincts

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:28.750
and treat him for poisoning

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:30.990
because that is the symptoms
that they are seeing.

00:03:30.990 --> 00:03:32.430
They put them on a ventilator

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:36.270
and they put him into a medically
induced coma to recover.

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:38.000
Over the next few days,

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:41.020
Alexei Navalny is in
the intensive care unit,

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:43.230
in a coma, in this hospital.

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:44.750
But the hospital starts to fill up,

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:45.730
not just with doctors

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:47.990
but Russian government officials

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:50.020
who start barring people like his wife

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:52.430
and his personal doctor
from entering the room.

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:55.960
Navalny and his family do not
feel safe in this hospital.

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:56.793
It's at this time

00:03:56.793 --> 00:03:59.280
that a German humanitarian
non-profit organization

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:01.310
offers to charter a jet

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:04.660
to fly him from this town
in Russia, out of Russia

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:06.179
to be treated in Berlin.

00:04:06.179 --> 00:04:08.390
(upbeat music)

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:10.240
Soon, he's on an airplane to Berlin

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:11.850
where he arrives at a hospital

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:14.550
and they run all of the
same poison blood tests

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:16.060
that they did in Russia,

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:19.463
but this time they find
that he was poisoned.

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:21.420
This would have come up

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:23.060
on the test they did in Russia,

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:24.550
but somebody decided

00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:26.340
not to reveal that to the doctors.

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:28.900
- Mr. Navalny remains in an induced coma

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:29.950
at a Berlin hospital.

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:32.040
- The German doctors are
seeing that the poison

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:34.570
that was somehow administered
to Alexei Navalny

00:04:34.570 --> 00:04:37.000
is some crazy nerve poison

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:39.840
that sends the victim
into a state of paralysis

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:43.070
and gives nerve damage,
and inducing seizures,

00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:45.160
and making their heart slow down.

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:46.500
It's a poison that was developed by

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:49.692
Soviet scientists during the Cold War.

00:04:49.692 --> 00:04:50.980
(cameras flashing)

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:53.340
And they used it to quietly attack people

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:54.420
they wanted to get rid of,

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:56.330
like spies or double agents.

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:59.350
It's called Novichok, and
it is a brutal poison,

00:04:59.350 --> 00:05:02.150
and it was the poison that
was used on Alexei Navalny.

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:03.640
- Tonight this incredible story,

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:06.270
the most prominent
Russian opposition leader

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:08.690
is in a coma on a ventilator.

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:11.120
- Now there's a lot of
ways to poison someone.

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:14.230
You can use ingredients
that anyone has access to.

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:16.940
Novichok is something
that is developed and used

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:19.920
only by the Russian
Military and Intelligence.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:21.730
In a sense, it's a signature,

00:05:21.730 --> 00:05:24.070
so Navalny goes back into
a medically induced coma

00:05:24.070 --> 00:05:25.570
in this hospital in Berlin

00:05:25.570 --> 00:05:27.850
where doctors are doing
their best to treat him

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:30.580
and also investigate what happened.

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:34.299
Soon, the world would know
exactly what happened.

00:05:34.299 --> 00:05:38.270
(recorder screeching)

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:39.690
Okay, let's just pause for a second.

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:42.170
Well, Alexei Navalny
is in a coma in Berlin

00:05:42.170 --> 00:05:44.190
because we need to ask
an important question

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:45.500
which is, who is this guy,

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:48.550
and why on earth is Soviet nerve poison

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:49.541
being used against him?

00:05:49.541 --> 00:05:51.750
(bright upbeat music)

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:53.310
For most of his adult life,

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:56.150
Alexei Navalny has been
dedicated to one thing,

00:05:56.150 --> 00:05:56.983
which is a shining light

00:05:56.983 --> 00:06:00.210
on how Russia really
works behind the scenes.

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:04.760
Not this or this, but how it really works.

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:06.770
One thing you need to know about Russia

00:06:06.770 --> 00:06:09.210
is that the whole society, the government,

00:06:09.210 --> 00:06:11.070
the business structures, everything,

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:14.440
is built on a giant
house of cards let's say.

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:16.520
It's delicate, it's fragile,

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:18.980
but it's the status quo

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:20.790
and Putin is at the top.

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:23.770
From there you have the
people closest to Putin's,

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:25.230
the ones that have his ear,

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:27.040
the rich Russian billionaires

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:29.070
who control Russia's main industries

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:32.030
like oil and gas, mining, telecoms,

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:34.040
all the richest guys in Russia.

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:35.620
These guys do favors for Putin

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:38.830
and Putin does favors for
them in the political sphere.

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:40.060
They scratch each other's back,

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:42.250
and in doing so, they maintain control

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:44.810
over everything that gets done in Russia.

00:06:44.810 --> 00:06:46.480
And this model repeats itself

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:48.710
as it trickles down to
regional governments

00:06:48.710 --> 00:06:50.920
and then to town and city governments

00:06:50.920 --> 00:06:53.310
who all operate in the same manner,

00:06:53.310 --> 00:06:55.000
keeping the society stable

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:58.750
through a culture of bribery,
secrecy, and intimidation.

00:06:58.750 --> 00:06:59.814
And it all happens in the name

00:06:59.814 --> 00:07:02.750
of keeping Putin secure in his position

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:03.950
so that he can in turn

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:05.600
keep his rich friends happy.

00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:08.750
The reason why Putin fears Alexei Navalny

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:11.510
is because Navalny wants all Russians

00:07:11.510 --> 00:07:14.040
to see exactly how this works,

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:15.470
to shine a light on it

00:07:15.470 --> 00:07:19.260
which could easily turn the
people against the system,

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:21.720
to knock down this house of cards

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:23.090
from the ground up,

00:07:23.090 --> 00:07:24.740
to stop putting up with a government

00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:27.020
that works for the rich corporate owners

00:07:27.020 --> 00:07:28.400
and not for the people.

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:31.180
And if this happens, it's Vladimir Putin

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:34.010
who has the longest hardest fall.

00:07:34.010 --> 00:07:35.670
Okay, but here's the
juiciest part of the story,

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:38.280
and the part that got me
into this and that I love,

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:41.070
which is that the tactics Navalny uses

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:43.970
to do this shine a light
on the system thing,

00:07:43.970 --> 00:07:45.700
there's no better way to
describe it than saying,

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:49.157
he's full on trolling Vladimir
Putin and his friends.

00:07:49.157 --> 00:07:52.657
(Alexei speaking Russian)

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:55.000
He does this in a lot of ways,

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:57.708
but what I love the most
are his well-produced

00:07:57.708 --> 00:08:00.420
internet explainer documentaries.

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:03.770
(Alexei speaking Russian)

00:08:03.770 --> 00:08:05.090
He makes these long videos

00:08:05.090 --> 00:08:07.040
exposing the indulgent corruption

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:08.210
of Russian billionaires

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:09.370
who control the country.

00:08:09.370 --> 00:08:12.010
And he uses these visual
investigation techniques

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:15.210
that are really stunning to
look at and really convincing.

00:08:15.210 --> 00:08:16.580
But there's also a good amount of

00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:19.780
snarky, poking fun in
every one of his videos

00:08:19.780 --> 00:08:20.940
like this deep dive

00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:23.490
into the corruption of
this Russian politician

00:08:23.490 --> 00:08:25.780
that starts with this goofy iPhone video

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:28.521
of him awkwardly dancing at
like a wedding or something.

00:08:28.521 --> 00:08:30.330
(man speaking Russian)

00:08:30.330 --> 00:08:31.880
But it's not just all poking fun,

00:08:31.880 --> 00:08:34.070
these videos then go very deep

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:38.160
and they reveal really useful
and compelling evidence

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:40.380
that shows just how bad this situation is,

00:08:40.380 --> 00:08:42.284
just how in bed the government is

00:08:42.284 --> 00:08:44.040
with these rich billionaires,

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:47.055
but always peppered with
a good amount of this.

00:08:47.055 --> 00:08:49.638
(upbeat music)

00:08:53.540 --> 00:08:56.280
He's like a viral internet sensation meets

00:08:56.280 --> 00:09:00.620
like, hardcore, journalists,
activists, video vlogger guy,

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:02.990
he's just an interesting character,

00:09:02.990 --> 00:09:04.070
so what is Navalny?

00:09:04.070 --> 00:09:06.930
He's kind of a politician,
but he's more than that.

00:09:06.930 --> 00:09:09.070
His specific policy agenda has more,

00:09:09.070 --> 00:09:11.190
and it's honestly like not that noble,

00:09:11.190 --> 00:09:13.790
like he totally supported
the annexation of Crimea

00:09:13.790 --> 00:09:15.800
which is like totally off limits

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:17.470
and a terrible thing that happened.

00:09:17.470 --> 00:09:20.200
And his electability as a
leader, isn't very likely

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:22.490
but that's not really at
the heart of his mission.

00:09:22.490 --> 00:09:24.140
His mission isn't about being elected,

00:09:24.140 --> 00:09:27.180
it's about dismantling the current system,

00:09:27.180 --> 00:09:28.910
not to convince people to vote for him,

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:31.950
but simply get people
to vote against Putin

00:09:31.950 --> 00:09:33.000
and the status quo.

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:34.507
And here's why this scares the

00:09:34.507 --> 00:09:35.340
(beep)

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:36.480
out of Vladimir Putin.

00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:38.310
Back to our house of cards,

00:09:38.310 --> 00:09:41.170
even though Putin is at
the top of this pyramid,

00:09:41.170 --> 00:09:43.050
it doesn't mean he's all powerful.

00:09:43.050 --> 00:09:45.590
He's not like a standard
totalitarian dictator

00:09:45.590 --> 00:09:47.760
who just has everyone under his thumb.

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:50.610
He's only powerful because
he's in the good graces

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:52.780
of all these super rich guys

00:09:52.780 --> 00:09:55.210
that own the massive companies of gas,

00:09:55.210 --> 00:09:57.630
telecoms, mining the
natural resources in Russia.

00:09:57.630 --> 00:10:00.380
If these guys turn on him, he's over.

00:10:00.380 --> 00:10:03.920
Putin, while powerful is simply one cog

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:06.440
in the machine of keeping
these guys powerful

00:10:06.440 --> 00:10:09.090
and immune from laws and regulation.

00:10:09.090 --> 00:10:09.923
Putin isn't afraid

00:10:09.923 --> 00:10:12.810
that all these YouTube
videos are going to create

00:10:12.810 --> 00:10:15.570
legal issues for Putin and his friends,

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:17.890
the courts in Russia
are just as influenced

00:10:17.890 --> 00:10:20.020
by this culture of
bribery and intimidation

00:10:20.020 --> 00:10:21.200
as everything else,

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:22.240
he's not afraid of that.

00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:25.010
Instead, he's afraid that
the people might realize

00:10:25.010 --> 00:10:26.760
that their government is controlled

00:10:26.760 --> 00:10:28.200
by a bunch of billionaires

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:31.585
and start demanding that
Russia be more transparent.

00:10:31.585 --> 00:10:34.668
(slow music playing)

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:38.140
Some accountability for these rich dudes

00:10:38.140 --> 00:10:39.870
and the leaders that support them.

00:10:39.870 --> 00:10:41.600
And like I said, if that happens,

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:42.690
these billionaires might be able

00:10:42.690 --> 00:10:44.130
to slip into the shadows

00:10:44.130 --> 00:10:46.120
and run away to some other country.

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:49.510
But Putin will be the
public face of the person

00:10:49.510 --> 00:10:50.930
who's kept this arrangement together,

00:10:50.930 --> 00:10:52.500
he will be enemy number one,

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:53.900
his fall will be the greatest

00:10:53.900 --> 00:10:55.400
that is why he's afraid.

00:10:55.400 --> 00:10:57.860
In a sense, he's painted
himself into a corner

00:10:57.860 --> 00:10:59.600
and he's past the point of no return.

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:01.820
He must maintain the current system

00:11:01.820 --> 00:11:03.500
or he will face the wrath of his people.

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:06.450
So far, the only person who has actually

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:08.920
garnered that wrath is Alexei Navalny.

